WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.801
-Hello, Jimmy.

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.267
Hello, audience.

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:05.534
Hello, legendary Roots crew.

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:07.267
-It is great to --
-Happy birthday, Ahmir.

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:08.400
-Thank you.

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:09.567
-It's coming up.
-Soon, soon.

00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:10.601
-Yeah, yeah,
it's coming up soon.

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:11.834
-Wow, you're good at that.

00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:13.601
-You know, you know,
just saying the hellos.

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:14.968
-Yeah.
-Just saying the hellos.

00:00:14.968 --> 00:00:16.934
-Are you good with
birthdays and all that stuff?

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:18.367
-No. No, no, no, no.
Not at all.

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:20.234
I don't remember anything.

00:00:20.234 --> 00:00:22.501
I mean, Apple has solved that
for all of us.

00:00:22.501 --> 00:00:23.801
-Yeah, exactly.

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:25.234
I feel like technology
has ruined remembering anything.

00:00:25.234 --> 00:00:26.267
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:27.133
-Oh, it says here
it's your birthday.

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:28.501
Happy birthday.

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:29.801
-I don't remember phone numbers
or birthdays anymore.

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:30.901
-Are you excited --
You're hosting the 80th annual

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:31.934
Golden Globe Awards
this Tuesday.

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:33.234
-Whoo!

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:34.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
It's a big deal.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.300
-Yeah.
-Are you excited?

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.567
-So, no, no.

00:00:37.567 --> 00:00:40.467
So, I was very excited.

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:41.467
-Yes.

00:00:41.467 --> 00:00:42.968
-Like, very, very excited.

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:45.534
Like, I remember
getting the call.

00:00:45.534 --> 00:00:47.968
I was at home.
I live in New York.

00:00:47.968 --> 00:00:50.000
I was alone for Christmas.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.501
I'm --

00:00:52.501 --> 00:00:56.000
I'm "don't go home
for Christmas" gay,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.334
which means that my mom
doesn't necessarily agree

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:02.567
with, like, my "gay lifestyle,"
in her words.

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:04.067
-Yeah.
-So -- And she wants me

00:01:04.067 --> 00:01:07.234
to come home for Christmas,
but I can't give Jesus that.

00:01:07.234 --> 00:01:08.667
Like, I know
it's his birthday...

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:11.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.534 --> 00:01:12.968
...but I just can't
let him have it.

00:01:12.968 --> 00:01:14.534
I can't let her have it.

00:01:14.534 --> 00:01:16.100
-No, you can't.
-You know what I mean?

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:18.601
Like, I just, like, you know,
as the old saying goes,

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:21.267
"Jesus is the reason
for your mother's homophobia."

00:01:21.267 --> 00:01:22.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:24.000
-I've seen that.
-So, I'm home.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.868
-I've seen that
on bumper stickers, yeah.

00:01:25.868 --> 00:01:28.033
-I'm home.

00:01:28.033 --> 00:01:29.501
I'm alone.

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:31.501
I'm, like, bored.

00:01:31.501 --> 00:01:33.267
I like to work.
-Yeah.

00:01:33.267 --> 00:01:34.701
-And I get the call.

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:36.334
They're like, "Do you want
to host the Golden Globes?"

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:38.534
And I said yes. I was very,
very excited to host.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:40.601
So, I was like, "Yeah,
this sounds amazing."

00:01:40.601 --> 00:01:43.067
And I was ready to begin
the process and the work.

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:46.634
And then I remembered

00:01:46.634 --> 00:01:52.267
that I'll have to be working
with my arch nemesis --

00:01:52.267 --> 00:01:53.934
NBC marketing.

00:01:53.934 --> 00:01:57.033
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.033 --> 00:01:58.033
-Wow.

00:01:58.033 --> 00:02:00.133
-Oh, how I hate NBC marketing.

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:02.467
You guys don't know.
You don't know.

00:02:02.467 --> 00:02:04.234
They're both lazy and pushy.

00:02:04.234 --> 00:02:06.267
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:08.267
Which is a hell of a combo.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:10.501
-Like, they're like,
"We have no ideas

00:02:10.501 --> 00:02:12.667
and we need
it done tomorrow by 5:00."

00:02:12.667 --> 00:02:14.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.334
-You were at --
You had a show you --

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:18.167
-Nothing.
They had nothing, Jimmy.

00:02:18.167 --> 00:02:19.868
-Yeah.
-They presented me --

00:02:19.868 --> 00:02:21.501
First of all, we have to do
billboards for the show,

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:23.834
'cause we got to tell people
the show's happening.

00:02:23.834 --> 00:02:25.767
So, they send me
a billboard --

00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:26.868
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:26.868 --> 00:02:28.334
-Which is
a recycled picture of me,

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:33.133
an old photo of me from "SNL,"
like, when I hosted.

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:34.868
Smiling. Big smile.

00:02:34.868 --> 00:02:36.667
They want you to smile.

00:02:36.667 --> 00:02:41.667
And they had a tagline
that said, "Changin' it up,"

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:43.000
without a "g."

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.734
'Cause you know how I speak.

00:02:44.734 --> 00:02:47.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.067
You know your boy,
known for dropping them "G's."

00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:54.367
That's a Black man
talking for you.

00:02:54.367 --> 00:02:56.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:59.000
-Changin' it up?
-Changin' it up.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.267
So, I said, obviously,

00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:01.868
"This is unacceptable."

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:04.000
-Oh, my God.
-And I said, you know,

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.200
"Why are we using an old photo?

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.834
You're a trillion-dollar
corporation."

00:03:06.834 --> 00:03:09.100
-Yeah.
-"Let's take a new picture."

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:10.901
They said, "Fine."

00:03:10.901 --> 00:03:14.701
And they said, "Can you smile,
you know, in the new picture,

00:03:14.701 --> 00:03:17.100
so we can put 'Changin' it up'
beside your face?"

00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:20.934
And I said, "How about I scowl,
and instead of 'Changin' it up,'

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:23.467
it says,
'A night of devastation'?"

00:03:23.467 --> 00:03:24.601
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.601 --> 00:03:26.067
And --

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:29.334
-Oh, my God.

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:31.100
-They said -- They said,
"What about

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:33.000
'An evening of joy
and devastation'?"

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.634
-And I said, "Fine."

00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:36.667
So, then I thought it was cool.

00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:38.267
Then it came time to do promos,

00:03:38.267 --> 00:03:40.534
'cause you've got to do,
like, shoot things.

00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:41.767
-Commercials.

00:03:41.767 --> 00:03:43.567
-Commercials and stuff
like that for the show.

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:46.167
So, their big idea

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:49.767
was for me to, once again, smile

00:03:49.767 --> 00:03:52.501
and say a bunch of corny jokes
into the camera

00:03:52.501 --> 00:03:55.100
about how I'm excited
to host the Golden Globes.

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:57.667
"It's going to be great.

00:03:57.667 --> 00:03:58.968
See you Tuesday at 8:00."

00:04:00.801 --> 00:04:04.334
And I said,
"What if instead of that,

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:08.367
I get Stone Cold Steve Austin
to yell at me

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:09.667
and, like, spit in my face

00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:12.000
and tell me how award shows
are meaningless

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.334
and how he's disappointed in me

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:16.334
for doing this
in the first place?"

00:04:16.334 --> 00:04:18.033
And they said,

00:04:18.033 --> 00:04:19.501
"No, we don't think
that represents

00:04:19.501 --> 00:04:22.033
the brand of the Golden Globes."

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:24.901
So then I said, "How about
I just don't do the show?"

00:04:24.901 --> 00:04:26.934
And then they said, "No, no,
we love Stone Cold."

00:04:26.934 --> 00:04:29.167
So, then --
Look, I even have on --

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:30.367
Look. I don't know
if you can see this.

00:04:30.367 --> 00:04:32.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.868
I'm a big -- that's Rattlesnake.

00:04:33.868 --> 00:04:36.100
-That's my dude.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.133
So, we got Stone Cold.

00:04:38.133 --> 00:04:40.200
They agreed to get me
Stone Cold.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.534
Then Stone Cold's dad died.

00:04:42.534 --> 00:04:44.033
I know. It was tragic.

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:46.801
But he agreed, but it was just
too much for him in the moment.

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:48.667
So we didn't have
Stone Cold anymore.

00:04:48.667 --> 00:04:50.234
So, then it was just me.
I said, okay.

00:04:50.234 --> 00:04:51.734
Well, fine.

00:04:51.734 --> 00:04:53.167
Maybe I could do some jokes.

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:54.667
You know, I'm not usually
that type of comedian

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:58.701
that just, like, is, you know,
punch line-heavy comic.

00:04:58.701 --> 00:05:01.033
But I was like, "I have
a few jokes that I could say."

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:02.734
You know, I have
this great one about --

00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:04.701
I don't know how to really
say this for television.

00:05:04.701 --> 00:05:10.167
It was one about how when
I give head,

00:05:10.167 --> 00:05:13.467
I look like Viola Davis
in an emotional scene.

00:05:13.467 --> 00:05:15.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.901 --> 00:05:18.000
You know what I mean?
It's just, like, wet.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.200
Just lip quivering
and the whole thing.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:24.100
[ Laughter continues ]

00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:26.767
And...

00:05:29.534 --> 00:05:30.400
-Oh, my God.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.968
-And then they said,

00:05:33.968 --> 00:05:35.567
"No, we don't think
that represents

00:05:35.567 --> 00:05:38.501
the brand of
the Golden Globes."

00:05:38.501 --> 00:05:39.934
Whatever.
-You think?

00:05:39.934 --> 00:05:41.067
-Whatever.
-Wow.

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:42.234
-Fine, fine.

00:05:42.234 --> 00:05:43.901
So, then, I pitched --
I was like, "Okay.

00:05:43.901 --> 00:05:45.133
Well, how about this?"

00:05:45.133 --> 00:05:48.534
I'll just speak honestly
and directly to camera

00:05:48.534 --> 00:05:49.968
and I'll talk about how, like,

00:05:49.968 --> 00:05:52.701
I know the Globes have gone
through a lot of controversy.

00:05:52.701 --> 00:05:54.734
They didn't air last year.

00:05:54.734 --> 00:05:55.901
Hollywood Foreign
Press Association

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:57.701
didn't have any Black members.

00:05:57.701 --> 00:06:01.000
And I said, "How about I just
speak, you know, truthfully,

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:05.501
directly to the camera about how
much Black approval means to me

00:06:05.501 --> 00:06:08.067
and how I hope Black people
don't boycott the show

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:10.467
and watch and, like,
give it a chance.

00:06:10.467 --> 00:06:13.434
And, like, you know,
I wanted to speak sincerely.

00:06:13.434 --> 00:06:15.000
And they said, "Okay, fine,
you can do that.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:18.534
But could you smile
while you said that?"

00:06:18.534 --> 00:06:21.334
And I said, "Absolutely not."

00:06:21.334 --> 00:06:23.067
So, then, this is the clip.

00:06:23.067 --> 00:06:25.167
-Here's the promo --
here's Jerrod Carmichael

00:06:25.167 --> 00:06:27.567
in a promo
for The Golden Globe Awards.

00:06:27.567 --> 00:06:28.968
Look at this.

00:06:28.968 --> 00:06:31.133
-My biggest fear is what will
Black people think of me,

00:06:31.133 --> 00:06:36.367
because Black acceptance means
a lot, means everything to me.

00:06:36.367 --> 00:06:39.567
I feel like Oprah never
viewed me as Black excellence,

00:06:39.567 --> 00:06:41.100
and that kind of haunts me.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.567
Oprah and my mother,

00:06:42.567 --> 00:06:44.100
the lack of acceptance
I received

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:45.234
from both of those women

00:06:45.234 --> 00:06:48.434
really causes me
a tremendous amount of pain,

00:06:48.434 --> 00:06:50.100
especially Oprah, though.

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:51.300
My mother, too,

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.334
but if we're being honest,
it's mainly Oprah.

00:06:53.334 --> 00:06:55.601
-Jerrod Carmichael hosts
The Golden Globe Awards,

00:06:55.601 --> 00:06:58.567
Tuesday on NBC
and streaming on Peacock.

00:06:58.567 --> 00:07:02.634
-What in the world?

00:07:02.634 --> 00:07:04.367
Dude, I think everyone's
going to be watching.

00:07:04.367 --> 00:07:06.067
By the way, this is the --

00:07:06.067 --> 00:07:08.234
This is the promo I saw.
This picture of you.

00:07:08.234 --> 00:07:10.000
-Just got to look.
It's going to be...

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:12.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
...a big night!

00:07:12.901 --> 00:07:14.267
-I can't wait. Break a leg.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:15.434
Thank you for coming
on the show.

00:07:15.434 --> 00:07:16.734
-You're the best, buddy.
-Thank you very much.

00:07:16.734 --> 00:07:17.767
-Jerrod Carmichael.

00:07:17.767 --> 00:07:19.667
Golden Globe Awards,
this Tuesday,

00:07:19.667 --> 00:07:22.100
8:00 p.m. on NBC and Peacock.

00:07:22.100 --> 00:07:24.100
Jessie Reyez performs
after the break.

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:25.167
Stick around, everybody.

